Here's an example implementation in R:
```R
# function to perform binary search on a sorted vector
binary_search <- function(sorted_vector, target) {
  low <- 1
  high <- length(sorted_vector)

  while(low <= high) {
    mid <- (low + high) / 2

    if(target == sorted_vector[mid]) {
      return(mid)
    } else if(target < sorted_vector[mid]) {
      high <- mid - 1
    } else {
      low <- mid + 1
    }
  }

  return(-1)
}
```
This function takes two arguments: `sorted_vector`, which should be a numeric vector containing only unique elements and ordered in ascending order, and `target`, which will be a single numeric value. 
